# Local development secrets for `npm run dev` (Vite + workerd).
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the keys you actually have.
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored; this example file is not, so never put a real key
# in here.
#
# IMPORTANT: these are read by the Worker (c.env), NOT by Vite. Do not move
# them into `.env` and do not prefix them with VITE_ - anything named VITE_* is
# inlined into the browser bundle, which would publish your key.
#
# In production these are Wrangler secrets instead:
#   npx wrangler secret put POE_API_KEY

# --- Keys: one per upstream account ----------------------------------------

# OpenCode Go (https://opencode.ai/go) - serves ChatGPT (GPT 5.6 Luna),
# DeepSeek, Kimi, Grok, and the free MiMo and Muse Spark tiers, plus MiniMax
# when its own key is missing or refused. One key, two protocols behind it.
# Muse Spark needs a one-time data-collection opt-in in the OpenCode
# workspace, or it answers 403 DataPolicyError.
OPENCODE_API_KEY=

# Poe (https://poe.com/api_key) - serves Claude; also Gemini when
# GEMINI_CHANNEL=poe (or for the interpretation pass when GOOGLE_API_KEY is
# unset), and ChatGPT when CHATGPT_CHANNEL=poe.
POE_API_KEY=

# Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) - Gemini's default
# channel (free-tier Flash).
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# MiniMax (https://platform.minimaxi.com) - first in MiniMax's default channel
# chain (minimax, then opencode). Leave it blank and MiniMax runs on OpenCode
# Go instead.
MINIMAX_API_KEY=

# --- Sign-in ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set locally. The deployed API only answers users signed in with
# Cloudflare Access (ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN / ACCESS_AUD in wrangler.jsonc, see
# README.md "Sign-in and rate limiting"); requests to localhost skip that
# check, so `npm run dev` and `npm run preview` work without it.

# --- Optional local overrides ----------------------------------------------
# The defaults are the production routing in worker/channels.ts; any var in
# `WorkerEnv` there can be set here to depart from it for local runs, e.g.:
#   GEMINI_CHANNEL=poe
#   CHATGPT_CHANNEL=poe
#   POE_CHATGPT_MODEL=gpt-5.4-pro
#   OPENCODE_GROK_MODEL=grok-4.5
#   NO_STREAM=deepseek                # only needed on the free Workers plan (10 ms CPU)
#   MINIMAX_CHANNEL=opencode          # MiniMax on the Go plan instead of your own key
#
# Check a key without spending tokens:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $POE_API_KEY" https://api.poe.com/v1/models
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENCODE_API_KEY" -H "x-opencode-session: any-uuid" https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/models
# A 401 means the key itself is rejected; the model name is a separate problem
# and shows up as a 404 or an "unknown model" message.
